From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <stefdo61@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:18:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 171/192] ath11k_nss: give the hybrid-bus radio its BAR and
 window offsets

The wifili init message hands the NSS firmware physical register
addresses: hssm.dev_base_addr is ab->mem_pa, and every ring's
hwreg_base[] is ab->mem_pa plus a window-translated offset
(ath11k_nss_fill_srng_info).

On a QCN6122 neither of the two is filled in. The chip is a hybrid-bus
device, so ath11k_ahb_setup_resources() takes the hybrid_bus_type branch
and never touches mem_pa - the DT reg is only the MSI address, and the
real BAR arrives later in the QMI device_info reply, where nothing stores
it. And ath11k_ahb_hif_ops_qcn6122 has no .get_window_offset, so
ath11k_hif_get_window_offset() returns the raw UMAC offset instead of the
window-relative one the host itself uses.

The firmware therefore receives ring registers at physical 0x00Axxxxx -
a bare offset with no base - and traps on the first transmit, which is
the first frame the VAP sends after it comes up (IPv6 MLD/NDP is enough;
no client is needed). Measured on a GL-B3000: without this the core dies
0.8 s after the VAP is up; with it the radio survives bring-up and the
firmware reports "hybrid bus BAR 0xa1e00000 size 0x200000".

Signed-off-by: Stefan <stefdo61@gmail.com>
[Andrei: Context drifted; hunks placed by unique match (2 with trimmed context).]
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c |  9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
index a65bc57..1784916 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
@@ -836,6 +836,25 @@ static const struct ath11k_hif_ops ath11k_ahb_hif_ops_wcn6750 = {
 	.ce_irq_disable = ath11k_pci_disable_ce_irqs_except_wake_irq,
 };
 
+/* The NSS firmware reaches this radio's ring registers through the same
+ * static windows the host does (UMAC in window 1, CE in window 2 - see
+ * ath11k_ahb_config_static_window_qcn6122()), so the offsets handed to it
+ * in the wifili init message must be window-relative. Without this hook
+ * ath11k_hif_get_window_offset() returns the raw register offset, which
+ * lies outside the mapped range, and the firmware programs rings that do
+ * not exist.
+ */
+static u32 ath11k_ahb_get_window_offset_qcn6122(struct ath11k_base *ab,
+						u32 offset)
+{
+	u32 window_start = ath11k_ahb_get_window_start_wcn6750(ab, offset);
+
+	if (window_start)
+		offset = window_start + (offset & ATH11K_PCI_WINDOW_RANGE_MASK);
+
+	return offset;
+}
+
 static const struct ath11k_hif_ops ath11k_ahb_hif_ops_qcn6122 = {
 	.start = ath11k_pcic_start,
 	.stop = ath11k_pcic_stop,
@@ -852,6 +871,7 @@ static const struct ath11k_hif_ops ath11k_ahb_hif_ops_qcn6122 = {
 	.ce_irq_enable = ath11k_pci_enable_ce_irqs_except_wake_irq,
 	.ce_irq_disable = ath11k_pci_disable_ce_irqs_except_wake_irq,
 	.config_static_window = ath11k_ahb_config_static_window_qcn6122,
+	.get_window_offset = ath11k_ahb_get_window_offset_qcn6122,
 };
 
 static int ath11k_core_get_rproc(struct ath11k_base *ab)
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
index 623a9cb..eec4ef5 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
@@ -2203,6 +2203,15 @@ static int ath11k_qmi_request_device_info(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 
 	ab->mem = bar_addr_va;
 	ab->mem_len = resp.bar_size;
+	/* The NSS wifili path hands the firmware physical register addresses
+	 * derived from mem_pa (hssm.dev_base_addr and every ring's
+	 * hwreg_base[]). On a hybrid-bus radio the BAR comes from this QMI
+	 * reply, not from the DTS, and nothing else fills mem_pa in - so the
+	 * firmware would be told the registers live at physical 0.
+	 */
+	ab->mem_pa = resp.bar_addr;
+	ath11k_info(ab, "hybrid bus BAR 0x%llx size 0x%x\n",
+		    (unsigned long long)resp.bar_addr, resp.bar_size);
 
 	if (!ab->hw_params.ce_remap)
 		ab->mem_ce = ab->mem;
